From cbc1e6e989485549935ae0d8e0a14d097cd1315d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caleb White <cdwhite3@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:40:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] bluez5: reset the transport error count on a successful
 acquire

error_count is only cleared by the TRANSPORT_ERROR_TIMEOUT check in
spa_bt_transport_acquire(), which compares against last_error_time. A
successful acquire in between does not clear it, so errors separated by
successful use accumulate to TRANSPORT_ERROR_MAX_RETRY and the next
acquire fails with -EIO.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5[1m]
(cherry picked from commit d80b80602b389fe9badeda830122d357e9e2e3ea)
---
 spa/plugins/bluez5/bluez5-dbus.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spa/plugins/bluez5/bluez5-dbus.c b/spa/plugins/bluez5/bluez5-dbus.c
index 34b39a98f..72f3c43c5 100644
--- a/spa/plugins/bluez5/bluez5-dbus.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/bluez5/bluez5-dbus.c
@@ -3452,6 +3452,8 @@ int spa_bt_transport_acquire(struct spa_bt_transport *transport, bool optional)
 	if (res >= 0) {
 		transport->acquire_refcount = 1;
 		transport->acquired = true;
+		/* a transport that acquires is working */
+		transport->error_count = 0;
 	}
 
 	return res;
